[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63384,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 207,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Adenomyoma is a mass formed by an admixture of endometrial-type glands (with or without endometrial stroma) and prominent smooth muscle.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:41:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63385,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 207,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8932/0 Adenomyoma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:41:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63386,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 207,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F38 &amp; XH4ZH4 Benign neoplasm of other or unspecified sites &amp; Adenomyoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:41:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63387,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 207,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> extrauterine adenomyoma</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> uterus-like mass; endomyometriosis</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:41:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63388,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 207,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:41:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63389,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 207,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Broad and other uterine ligaments</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:41:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63390,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 207,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients may present with abdominal pain, a pelvic mass, and/or vaginal bleeding {23532253; 16175086}. Rarely, the tumour is discovered many years after hysterectomy and bilateral salpingo-oophorectomy {16048397}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:41:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63391,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 207,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This is an uncommon tumour. The average patient age is about 50&nbsp;years, but some cases occur in young women {22413810; 19047912; 23532253}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:41:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63392,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 207,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:41:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63393,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 207,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Extrauterine adenomyoma may be a result of failure of complete fusion of M&uuml;llerian ducts and is occasionally associated with other congenital urogenital abnormalities. It may also be due to coelomic metaplasia {22413810; 16048397}. Some lesions are considered smooth muscle metaplasia surrounding a focus of endometriosis {17592255; 3838644}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:41:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63394,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 207,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Adenomyomas are circumscribed and well demarcated from the surrounding structures. The median size is 5.5&nbsp;cm. Adenomyoma resembles leiomyoma with a whorled cut surface but also with scattered small cysts or foci of haemorrhage {22413810; 19047912; 10907166}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:41:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63395,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 207,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The mass consists of endometrial-type glands and stroma scattered throughout a background of smooth muscle {12075412; 16048397}. Smooth muscle cells with bizarre nuclei have been described {19047912}. Cases in which the endometrial-type epithelium and stroma form a central cyst surrounded by smooth muscle may resemble a uterus (a so-called uterus-like mass).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:41:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63396,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 207,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:41:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63397,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 207,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:41:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63398,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 207,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> endometrial-type glands and stroma within a mass of smooth muscle.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:41:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63399,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 207,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:41:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63400,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 207,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Adenomyomas are benign, but rare cases of adenocarcinoma have been reported {1879815; 24942896}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:41:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]